<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Dou Jiande</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">573–621</span> · <a href="/centuries/7th-century">7th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Dou Jiande was a rebel leader during the collapse of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sui-dynasty">Sui dynasty</a> who built a kingdom called Xia on the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hebei">Hebei</a> plain, known for its humane treatment of captives. Marching to relieve <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/wang-shichong">Wang Shichong</a> at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/luoyang">Luoyang</a> in 621, he was defeated and captured by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/emperor-taizong-of-tang">Li Shimin</a> at the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-hulao">Battle of Hulao</a> and executed by the Tang.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/dou-jiande.jpg" alt="Dou Jiande" width="320" height="457" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown authorUnknown author · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:%E7%AB%87%E5%BB%BA%E5%BE%B7%EF%BC%88%E8%AA%AA%E5%94%90%E6%BC%94%E7%BE%A9%E5%85%A8%E5%82%B3%EF%BC%89.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
